--- body ---
## Context

The author wants adversarial smoke testing of the plugin, not just the
happy-path DOM/style smoke that already exists (per ticket 0686's own
note: "the existing DOM/style smoke does not establish keyboard or
screen-reader behavior" -- the same gap applies to the scheduler's
failure handling).

`scheduler.js`'s `createSDTSitter(host)` already takes an injectable
`host.now()` for every timestamp, and `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`'s
fixture already injects a fake clock -- confirmed in code, not to-add.
The four scenarios below are testable today, in the same style as the
existing seven tests in that file, with no new harness and no dependency
on ticket 0689's journal (assert against `host.reportError` calls and
scheduler state directly; do not invent a dependency on an unbuilt
journal for scenarios that don't need one).

## Scenarios

| Scenario | Fake | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| Worker rejects mid-job | `ensure()` rejects after 3 progress ticks | Suppressed by source/processor identity; next document admitted; `host.reportError` called once |
| Worker resolves, pack absent/corrupt | `inspect` finds nothing | Not counted as coverage; treated as a failure, not a silent success -- check this isn't a near-duplicate of the existing "native success without persisted cache counts as failure" test before writing it |
| Disk crosses threshold mid-job | resource reading goes from comfortable to below-threshold between admissions | Current job continues uninterrupted (admission-time check, not a running cap); the next admission is refused |
| Disable during active job | `stop()`/shutdown called while a submission is pending | No further `submit` after the call; the pending promise is not force-cancelled |

Worker-process death itself (kill the worker, not just reject a promise)
is out of scope -- that is ticket 0681's crash-recovery detection.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Each row is one test, shown red once against a deliberately broken
      scheduler -- record the red commit hash in this ticket's log.
- [ ] Tests run under this repo's existing `make check` (no separate
      "integration tier" selector exists in this project's Makefile/
      conftest -- tag with the registered `integration` marker for
      classification only, it is not a gate).
- [ ] Each test is checked against the existing seven in
      `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs` for overlap before being counted as
      new coverage.
